spire: serve the telemetry of the SPIRE server and agent to Prometheus

server.conf and agent.conf have no telemetry block, so no SPIRE metric reaches Prometheus. Two incidents need
SPIRE's own numbers:
  - #34, and the outage of 2026-10-25: SPIRE activated a CA that the issuer approval did not pin. The server sets
    manager.x509_ca.rotate.expiration (notAfter of the CA it activated last) and manager.x509_ca.rotate.max_expiration
    (the later notAfter of the active and the prepared CA) per trust domain: SPIRE fork 0f8fe4d681,
    pkg/common/telemetry/server/ca_manager.go:42-55 and :66-73.
  - #42: ztunnel fetches workload certificates in bursts. The agent counts each DelegatedIdentity call by its gRPC
    status when the call ends: rpc.delegated_identity.subscribe_to_x509_svids (pkg/common/api/middleware/metrics.go,
    middleware/interceptor.go). ztunnel ends each SubscribeToX509SVIDs stream after the first answer, so the
    counter counts fetches.

The patch appends the same block to both configurations and declares it as the container port "prom":

    telemetry {
      Prometheus {
        host = "0.0.0.0"
        port = 9988
      }
    }

Host 0.0.0.0, port 9988 and the port name "prom" are those of the SPIFFE hardened Helm chart
(spiffe/helm-charts-hardened, charts/spire/charts/spire-server/templates/configmap.yaml and
charts/spire/charts/spire-agent/values.yaml and templates/daemonset.yaml, read 2026-10-27). The Prometheus names
are the keys joined by "_" under spire_server or spire_agent: spire_server_manager_x509_ca_rotate_expiration,
spire_server_manager_x509_ca_rotate_max_expiration, spire_agent_rpc_delegated_identity_subscribe_to_x509_svids.
A counter keeps its key without "_total" (hashicorp/go-metrics v0.7.0 prometheus/prometheus.go, Name: key). Every
series carries a host label: SPIRE turns EnableHostnameLabel on by default (pkg/common/telemetry/metrics.go:87).

Decisions for the operator:
  1. Exposure. The endpoint is plain HTTP. The server listens in its Pod's network namespace. The agent runs with
     hostNetwork, so it listens on every address of its node, as its health checks on 4251 do already: a client
     that reaches a node address on 9988 reads the agent's metrics (call counts by method and status, the node's
     hostname, Go runtime figures; no key material). Namespace cilium-spire has no NetworkPolicy. SPIRE can serve
     the endpoint over TLS with its own SVID and a list of authorized SPIFFE IDs (tls { use_spire_svid = true
     authorized_spiffe_ids = [...] }, pkg/common/telemetry/prometheus.go); the Prometheus of
     observability/v2/deploy then needs an SVID of its own.
  2. Rollout. SPIRE reads its configuration at start, so the server and every agent restart. The live agents do
     not mount the spire-agent ConfigMap this renderer writes: they mount cmtc-delegated-agent-1f9ab66bbf7f5cd6
     (cmtc-a) and cmtc-delegated-agent-0da33e582bf1a6d5 (cmtc-b), labelled
     security.cmtc.io/owner=claude-delegated-socket, which no file of this repository renders (read with kubectl
     get on 2026-10-27T02:3xZ). Those ConfigMaps need the same block until their configuration is ported into the
     repository. workload_api.py make_plan refuses a live spire-agent ConfigMap that differs from agent_config()
     (workload_api.py:133): apply the new baseline ConfigMap before it runs again.

observability/v2/deploy scrapes the "prom" port when jobs.spireServer.enabled and jobs.spireAgent.enabled are
true; observability/v2/rules/proposed/spire-telemetry.rules.yaml holds the CA and fetch-storm rules.

